# Fuzz corpora are binary. A seed's trailing byte is the atheris selector
# (ConsumeIntInRange reads from the back of the buffer) and its leading byte
# is the string_spec, so any line-ending normalisation re-points the seed at
# a different grammar or edit plan without changing anything a diff shows.
fuzz/corpus/** binary
# Recorded answers are compared byte for byte: a file the repository holds
# with CRLF line ends is read back with them, so no checkout may convert one.
fixtures/reference_answers/** -text
